     sections=[["Everything under one roof", "<p>Most Hampton Roads businesses do not have a marketing problem so much as a fragmentation problem: one freelancer for the website, a cousin for social, a national platform for ads, and nobody owning the whole picture. Extra Medium replaces the patchwork with one senior team. <b>Strategy</b> comes first, then the full mix underneath it: <b>digital marketing</b>, <b>SEO</b>, <b>paid search and paid social</b>, <b>social media</b>, <b>influencer and creator marketing</b>, <b>content</b>, <b>creative and branding</b>, <b>web design</b>, <b>email</b>, and <b>fractional CMO leadership</b> for companies that need a senior seat filled part-time. The whole menu is on our <a href='/services/'>services page</a>; the point is that one team plans it, makes it and answers for it.</p>"], ["One market wearing seven name tags", "<p>Hampton Roads is seven cities &mdash; Virginia Beach, Norfolk, Chesapeake, Hampton, Newport News, Portsmouth and Suffolk &mdash; that behave like a single market with a lot of bridges. Naval Station Norfolk and the wider military economy, the Port of Virginia, the shipyard in Newport News, Sentara and the health systems, and Oceanfront tourism all pull customers across city lines every day. A restaurant lives in Virginia Beach and fills tables from Chesapeake. A contractor sits in Hampton and bids work in Suffolk. Families arrive on orders knowing nobody and search for everything. Marketing built for one zip code misses most of that; marketing built for the region catches it.</p>"], ["Senior people, plain talk", "<p>The practice is founder-led and senior-only: the person you meet is the person doing the work, and the advice is tested first on our own products in <a href='/labs/'>Extra Medium Labs</a>, where we build and run real businesses of our own. That tends to keep recommendations honest. If a channel would not survive contact with our own budget, it does not get recommended for yours.</p>"]],
     faqs=[["What size businesses does Extra Medium work with in Hampton Roads?", "The range is wide: single-location businesses selling across the seven cities, regional companies with several locations, and larger organizations that need senior marketing leadership without building a department first. The common thread is an owner or leadership team that wants the whole system run, not another vendor added to the pile."], ["Do you work with military-focused and defense-adjacent businesses?", "Yes. The military is the region&rsquo;s largest economic fact, between active-duty families, veterans, civilian employees and the contractors who support the bases and the shipyard. Marketing here has to respect how that audience actually lives: moves every few years, decisions made fast, and a sharp nose for being talked down to."], ["How do we start?", "Write to us through the <a href='/contact/'>contact page</a> and tell us what you are trying to grow. The first conversation is free and specific: whether we can help, what we would do first, and what it would cost, in writing. If we are not the right fit, we will say so plainly."]],
     takeaways=["Hampton Roads is one market with seven name tags; your marketing has to cross the river, the bay and the tunnel.", "One senior team for strategy, search, social, paid and creative beats five vendors pointing at each other.", "The person you meet is the person on your account. That is the whole staffing model."],
     keys=["marketing agency Hampton Roads", "Hampton Roads marketing agency", "Virginia Beach marketing agency", "Norfolk marketing agency", "digital marketing Hampton Roads", "fractional CMO Hampton Roads", "SEO Hampton Roads", "creator marketing Hampton Roads"],
