dict(slug="digital-marketing-agency-hampton-roads",
     title="Digital Marketing Agency in Hampton Roads | Extra Medium",
     hero="collage-labs",
     q="What does a digital marketing agency in Hampton Roads actually do for a local business?",
     desc="Digital marketing in Hampton Roads: SEO, paid search and social, social media, email, content and websites, run as one system by Extra Medium and measured against revenue.",
     answer="Extra Medium is a marketing agency in Hampton Roads, and digital is where this region does its shopping, hiring and trip-planning. We run the full digital mix: SEO, paid search and paid social, social media, email, content and websites that convert, measured against revenue instead of impressions and likes.",
     sections=[["The full mix, run as one system", "<p>Digital marketing fails in pieces. A business boosts a post here, runs a search ad there, sends an email when someone remembers, and wonders why the total feels like weather instead of climate. We run the channels as one system: <b>SEO</b> so you are found when people look, <b>paid search and paid social</b> to buy the demand you cannot wait for, <b>social media</b> to stay present between purchases, <b>email</b> to bring people back, <b>content</b> that gives all of it something worth saying, and a <b>website</b> built to turn the visit into a call, a booking or a sale. What each piece includes is laid out on our <a href='/services/'>services page</a>.</p>"], ["Built for how this region actually moves", "<p>Hampton Roads has rhythms most agencies never see. Every summer, thousands of military families arrive on orders and search for dentists, schools, gyms and realtors before the moving truck does. Tourists plan Oceanfront trips weeks out, on phones, comparing everything. Shipyard and defense employers recruit in a permanent labor shortage, and their candidates search like consumers. And locals commute across seven cities daily, so the customer in Norfolk at noon is the customer in Chesapeake by six. Digital campaigns here have to be timed and targeted for all four audiences at once, which is exactly how we build them.</p>"], ["Measured like owners, not vendors", "<p>Every engagement reports against revenue: calls, bookings, sales and pipeline, traced back to the channel that produced them. Activity metrics are fine for a dashboard and useless for a decision. If a channel is producing reports instead of customers, we say so and move the money &mdash; the same standard we run on our own products, and the same one behind our <a href='/fractional-cmo/'>fractional CMO</a> work when a company needs the strategy seat filled above the channels.</p>"]],
     faqs=[["Which digital channel should a Hampton Roads business start with?", "Whichever one sits closest to the money. If people already search for what you sell, start with search: SEO and paid search catch existing demand. If your offer needs explaining or showing, social and content usually lead. We sequence channels by payback, not by what is fashionable."], ["Do you rebuild websites, or only market them?", "Both. A slow or confusing website taxes every other channel, so web design and conversion work are part of the practice. Sometimes that is a rebuild; often it is fixing the five pages that carry most of the traffic."], ["How do we start?", "Send a note through the <a href='/contact/'>contact page</a> with what you sell and where it is stuck. We reply in writing with what we would look at first and what an engagement would look like. No pressure, no phone tag."]],
     takeaways=["In Hampton Roads, your next customer is often searching from another city, another state, or a ship headed home.", "Digital channels work as a system or not at all: search catches intent, social creates it, email keeps it.", "Impressions are weather. Revenue is climate. We report on climate."],
     keys=["digital marketing agency Hampton Roads", "digital marketing Virginia Beach", "paid search Hampton Roads", "PPC Norfolk VA", "online marketing Hampton Roads", "email marketing Hampton Roads", "web design Virginia Beach", "social media Hampton Roads"],
     iso="2026-11-15",
     market="Hampton Roads"),
dict(slug="seo-agency-hampton-roads",
     title="SEO Agency in Hampton Roads | Extra Medium",
     hero="collage-home",
     q="How does an SEO agency in Hampton Roads get you found across all seven cities?",
     desc="SEO for Hampton Roads businesses: local search, Google Business Profiles, technical health and content that ranks across Virginia Beach, Norfolk, Chesapeake and the whole region.",
     answer="Extra Medium is a marketing agency in Hampton Roads, and our SEO work is built for how this region actually searches: across seven city lines, on phones, with intent. We handle technical SEO, local search and Google Business Profiles, and content that ranks, so customers find you before the business across the tunnel.",
     sections=[["Local SEO for a region, not a zip code", "<p>Most local SEO is sold one city at a time, which is a poor fit for a region where nobody shops that way. A homeowner in Chesapeake searches for a plumber, a roofer or a pediatric dentist and happily hires from Norfolk or Virginia Beach; Google knows this, and its results cross city lines constantly. We build for the region: accurate and active <b>Google Business Profiles</b>, location and service pages written for each city you genuinely serve, reviews handled like the ranking asset they are, and the technical foundation &mdash; speed, structure, clean internal linking &mdash; that lets all of it count. The full picture of how SEO sits inside the practice is on our <a href='/services/'>services page</a>.</p>"], ["Tourists, newcomers and neighbors search differently", "<p>Hampton Roads has three search audiences with almost nothing in common. Tourists search the Oceanfront in bursts, comparing hotels, restaurants and things to do, mostly on phones and mostly in season. New military families search for an entire life at once &mdash; housing, schools, doctors, churches &mdash; from another state, before they arrive. Neighbors search the way everyone does: near me, open now, best rated. Each audience needs different pages, different words and different proof, and a single generic city page serves none of them well. We map the searches first, then build the content to match.</p>"], ["No guarantees, just compounding", "<p>SEO is the channel that keeps working while you sleep, but it is not instant and it is not magic. Rankings follow usefulness: pages that answer the search better than the page above them, on a site fast and organized enough for Google to trust. We report movement in rankings, calls and direction requests alongside revenue, so you can watch the asset build instead of taking anyone&rsquo;s word for it.</p>"]],
     faqs=[["How long does SEO take to work?", "Local SEO usually shows movement in weeks on profiles and existing pages, and months on competitive rankings. It compounds: the work done this quarter is still producing next year, which is why we treat it as building an asset rather than renting attention."], ["Can you guarantee we will rank first?", "No, and you should be suspicious of anyone who does. Google&rsquo;s results shift with location, history and season, especially in a tourism market. What we can guarantee is the work: technical health, complete profiles, and content built to be the best answer to the searches that pay."], ["How do we start?", "Write to us via the <a href='/contact/'>contact page</a> and tell us what you want to be found for. We will look at where you stand now and reply in writing with what we would fix first."]],
     takeaways=["Nobody in Hampton Roads searches inside one city line, so your SEO cannot stop at one either.", "Rankings follow usefulness: answer the search better than the page above you.", "Any agency guaranteeing you the top spot is selling you the spot, not the work."],
     keys=["SEO agency Hampton Roads", "SEO Virginia Beach", "local SEO Norfolk", "Google Business Profile Hampton Roads", "SEO company Chesapeake", "search engine optimization Hampton Roads", "SEO Newport News", "local search Hampton Roads"],
     iso="2026-11-15",
     market="Hampton Roads"),
dict(slug="social-media-marketing-hampton-roads",
     title="Social Media Marketing in Hampton Roads | Extra Medium",
     hero="collage-extra",
     q="What does social media marketing in Hampton Roads look like when it is done locally?",
     desc="Social media marketing in Hampton Roads from Extra Medium: planned, produced content plus local creator marketing through Magpie, our own platform for booking creators whose followers live here.",
     answer="Extra Medium is a marketing agency in Hampton Roads, and we treat social media as a local medium, because here it is one. We plan and run social content, and through our own lab we build Magpie, a platform that connects local businesses with local creators whose followers actually live nearby.",
     sections=[["A word-of-mouth region, at feed speed", "<p>Hampton Roads runs on who you know: base communities, school networks, church groups, shipyard crews, neighborhood pages. Social media is that grapevine with better distribution. We plan and produce content built for it &mdash; the faces, places and small specifics people here recognize as theirs &mdash; on a steady cadence instead of the usual burst of posts followed by silence. The strategy and production side of the work sits inside our wider <a href='/services/'>services</a>, so social pulls in the same direction as your search, email and offers instead of freelancing.</p>"], ["Creators who actually live here", "<p>Influencer marketing usually fails locally because the audience is somewhere else: a million followers spread across forty states is a billboard in the wrong town. Our lab builds <a href='/labs/magpie/'>Magpie</a>, a local creator marketing platform where businesses book creators by the followers they have in this market, not their total count. A Virginia Beach creator whose audience is Virginia Beach families is worth more to a Virginia Beach business than a national name, and the work costs a fraction as much. That local-reach thinking shapes every creator recommendation we make, on or off the platform.</p>"], ["Content that sounds like here", "<p>The fastest way to look like an outsider in this market is to sound like one: stock beaches, generic military appreciation, city names used interchangeably. We write and produce in the region&rsquo;s actual voice &mdash; Oceanfront in season and locals-only the rest of the year, the tunnel traffic everyone jokes about because everyone lives it, the pride people take in the fleet and the yard. Recognition is the whole game on social, and recognition is local or it is nothing.</p>"]],
     faqs=[["Do you create the content, or do we have to supply it?", "We plan, write, design and schedule it. You approve and supply the raw material only you have: the day-to-day photos, the team, the work itself. Most clients spend less time on social with us running it than they did doing it themselves."], ["Which platforms should a Hampton Roads business be on?", "Where your customers already are, which here usually means Instagram and Facebook first, with TikTok and YouTube earning their place depending on the audience. We would rather run two platforms properly than five at a whisper."], ["How do we start?", "Send a message through the <a href='/contact/'>contact page</a> telling us what you sell and who it is for. We reply in writing with the platforms and approach we would start with."]],
     takeaways=["In Hampton Roads the feed is the front porch: people buy from businesses their neighbors vouch for.", "A local creator with a few thousand neighbors beats a national influencer with a million strangers.", "Social works when it sounds like the place it is selling to. Here, that sound is specific."],
     keys=["social media marketing Hampton Roads", "social media agency Virginia Beach", "influencer marketing Hampton Roads", "local creators Hampton Roads", "Magpie", "content marketing Norfolk", "social media management Virginia Beach", "creator marketing"],
     iso="2026-11-15",
     market="Hampton Roads"),
