     sections=[["The full mix, run as one system", "<p>Digital channels are usually bought separately and blamed individually. We run them as one system with one owner: <b>SEO</b> so you are found when Richmond searches, <b>paid search and paid social</b> to buy demand on a deadline, <b>social media</b> to stay in the conversation between purchases, <b>email</b> to bring past customers back at almost no cost, <b>content</b> that gives every channel something credible to say, and a <b>website</b> built to convert the visit instead of admire it. How the pieces fit together is detailed on our <a href='/services/'>services page</a>.</p>"], ["Built for how Richmond actually buys", "<p>This is a research city. VCU students and the health system&rsquo;s workforce live online; state government and the finance and insurance sector run on careful, documented decisions; and the food and brewery scene &mdash; Carytown, Scott&rsquo;s Addition, a restaurant row worth arguing about &mdash; is chosen almost entirely from phones. The region is also a logistics crossroads at I-95 and I-64, so plenty of Richmond marketing is business-to-business, aimed at buyers who Google first and ask a colleague second. Campaigns built here have to satisfy the researcher and survive the referral check that follows.</p>"], ["Measured like owners, not vendors", "<p>We report against revenue and pipeline: calls, bookings, applications, sales. Dashboards full of impressions and engagement are weather reports; owners need climate. When a channel stops producing, we say so and move the money, and when the problem is strategy rather than channels, we will tell you that too &mdash; it is the same judgment our <a href='/fractional-cmo/'>fractional CMO</a> clients hire when they need the seat above the spend filled.</p>"]],
     faqs=[["Which channel should a Richmond business start with?", "The one closest to revenue. If buyers already search for what you sell, SEO and paid search lead. If your market needs warming up first &mdash; a new restaurant, a new service, a new name &mdash; social and content usually go first. We sequence by payback, and we will show you the reasoning."], ["Do you handle business-to-business marketing, or only consumers?", "Both, and Richmond demands it: logistics, professional services, healthcare and government-adjacent suppliers all sell to other organizations here. B2B digital is slower and more credibility-driven, and the system adjusts: content and search carry more weight, social warms a longer cycle."], ["How do we start?", "Send a note through the <a href='/contact/'>contact page</a> with what you sell and where it is stuck. We reply in writing with what we would examine first and what an engagement would look like."]],
