     sections=[["Digital, run as one system", "<p>SEO, paid search, paid social, email, content and web are one system here, planned together and reported together, as laid out on our <a href=\"/services/\">services page</a>. Run separately, each channel optimizes for its own report and the seams show: ads promising what the landing page does not say, content nobody can find, email lists built by accident. Run as a system, the search result, the ad and the page tell one story, and the budget moves toward whichever piece of it is producing members, registrations, donors or customers.</p>"], ["Built for how DC decides", "<p>DC audiences research before they commit. A prospective member reads the dues page, the annual report and three years of your conference content. A contractor gets vetted by people who check references for a living. A staffer deciding whether your event is worth an evening has a hundred options and a finely tuned filter. Digital marketing here has to survive that research: accurate pages, sourced claims, content with a point of view, and sites that load like you respect the reader&rsquo;s time &mdash; because in this city, the reader notices.</p>"], ["Measurement a board can read", "<p>Every engagement reports against outcomes a board, a CFO or an executive director actually cares about: memberships, registrations, donations, qualified inquiries, revenue. Impressions and clicks appear in the appendix, where they belong. If a channel cannot be connected to an outcome, we say so and either fix the tracking or stop the spend. That discipline is most of the job; the dashboards are the easy part.</p>"]],
     faqs=[["Which digital channels matter most in Washington DC?", "It depends on the audience, but the pattern is consistent: search and content carry the research phase, email carries the relationship, and paid media buys speed when a date matters &mdash; a conference, a membership drive, a comment deadline. Social supports all three. Anyone who answers before asking what you sell is guessing with your money."], ["How long does digital marketing take to show results?", "Paid media can produce signal in weeks. SEO and content compound over quarters. Email works as fast as the list you have earned. An honest plan says which is which up front, with early indicators to watch while the compounding builds."], ["How do we start?", "In writing. Send the problem through our contact page and you will get a specific reply: whether we can help, what we would do first, and what it would cost. Nobody books a call on your calendar unless you ask for one."]],
     takeaways=["Digital channels are one system. Run them separately and you pay for the seams.", "DC audiences research before they commit. Your content has to survive the research.", "If a metric cannot be spent, banked or renewed, it is not the headline."],
     keys=["digital marketing agency Washington DC", "DC digital marketing", "SEO Washington DC", "paid search DC", "association digital marketing", "nonprofit digital marketing", "DMV digital marketing"],
     iso="2026-11-15",
