     sections=[["A city that chooses on screens", "<p>Two of Wilmington&rsquo;s biggest audiences arrive pre-sold on searching. The newcomer, unpacking in Ogden or Leland, needs a dentist, a roofer, a gym and a brunch spot, and has no cousin to ask. The visitor, planning a Wrightsville week from Charlotte or Raleigh, builds the whole trip on a phone. Even lifelong locals switch to search the moment they need something new. The moment of choice in this market is a results page and a review profile, and digital marketing is the discipline of being the obvious answer in both.</p>"], ["The channels, and the job each one does", "<p>Paid search takes the intent that already exists: the near-me searches and the service-plus-city searches from people ready to book, buy or call. Paid social creates demand and can be aimed with local precision, by neighborhood and interest, from downtown to Mayfaire to the beach towns. Email turns first-timers into regulars, which is where the profit in hospitality and retail actually lives. Your website is where all of it lands, so it has to load fast, answer plainly and make the next step obvious on a phone. Retargeting ties the journey together for visitors who looked in March and book in May. Our <a href='/services/'>services</a> page covers the full digital mix.</p>"], ["Measured like owners", "<p>Budgets get sized from the value of a customer in your category, not from a package, and reporting runs against revenue, bookings and appointments in plain language. Channels that produce get fed; channels that do not get stopped, and we will tell you which is which. In a market growing this fast, the waste is not standing still. It is spending on activity nobody is judging.</p>"]],
