     sections=[["The full mix, one team", "<p>Strategy, digital marketing, SEO, paid search and paid social, social media, influencer and creator marketing, content, creative and branding, web design, email and fractional CMO leadership &mdash; the whole shelf, run by one senior team instead of five vendors who never meet. That is the <a href=\"/services/\">studio</a>: six practices under one roof, so the person setting the strategy is in the room when the work ships.</p><p>For most Roanoke companies the honest problem is not a missing channel. It is five channels running five different stories. One team fixes that: one plan, one calendar, one set of numbers everyone answers to.</p>"], ["Marketing in a word-of-mouth town", "<p>Roanoke runs on reputation. Carilion anchors a healthcare economy, the Blue Ridge Parkway and the Appalachian Trail bring a steady river of visitors past the Mill Mountain Star, and everybody else seems to know somebody you went to school with. In a market like this, marketing cannot fake it for long &mdash; the town compares notes. What works is senior thinking at a scale the market can carry: clear positioning, search and social that show up where locals actually look, and creative that sounds like a neighbor instead of a national chain. When the gap is leadership rather than labor, our <a href=\"/fractional-cmo/\">fractional CMO</a> practice fills the seat part-time.</p>"], ["How an engagement starts", "<p>One conversation, in writing first if you prefer. Bring the business problem &mdash; slow referrals, a website that ranks for nothing, a tourism season you keep missing &mdash; and we will tell you plainly whether we can help, what we would do first, and what it would cost, in writing, before any work begins. Diagnosis before prescriptions. If we are not the right fit for a Roanoke budget, we will say so and point you somewhere better.</p>"]],
     faqs=[["What does a marketing agency actually do for a small Roanoke business?", "It sets the strategy and runs the channels: your website and search presence, paid media, social, content and creative, all pointed at the same customers. The point of one agency is that the pieces stop contradicting each other."], ["Do we need a big-city budget to work with an agency?", "No. Engagements come in three shapes &mdash; fractional leadership, defined projects and ongoing growth &mdash; and the shape follows the problem and the budget, not the other way around. What matters is senior people and a written plan, not a big retainer."], ["How do we start?", "Start on the contact page with a few lines about the business and the problem. A human reads every note and replies within one business day with next steps, in writing. No call is required to get a straight answer."]],
     takeaways=["In Roanoke, reputation is the media plan. Marketing has to deserve the word of mouth it gets.", "Senior strategy and the full digital mix, without big-market retainer bloat.", "One team for strategy, creative and channels, so nothing gets lost between vendors."],
     keys=["marketing agency Roanoke VA", "Roanoke digital marketing", "Blue Ridge marketing agency", "small business marketing Roanoke", "fractional CMO Virginia", "SEO Roanoke", "paid media Roanoke"],
     iso="2026-11-15",
